;; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
;; keepassxc_spawn_isolation.cil — domain-inheritance breaker for helper spawns.
;;
;; When keepassxc_t executes a bin_t helper (for example, opening a stored
;; entry URL launches the browser via /usr/bin/flatpak, which execs bwrap and
;; the browser binary), the spawned process tree would inherit keepassxc_t.
;; Combined with the keepassxc_dbtype_autotrans rule that would be a hazard:
;; the inherited keepassxc_t helper creates files in user_home_t directories
;; (the browser profile tree), and the autotrans rule relabels every one of
;; them keepassxc_db_t — a cross-tree mislabel cascade.
;;
;; This module keeps the keepassxc_t sub-domain scoped to KeePassXC itself.
;; The type_transition kicks any bin_t exec from keepassxc_t back to staff_t,
;; so the helper chain runs entirely under staff_t and the autotrans rule does
;; not fire for files those helpers create. The two allows grant the execute
;; and the process-transition surface the kick-back requires.
;;
;; Target type is scoped to bin_t only: on a merged /usr/sbin host the helper
;; binaries (flatpak, bwrap, xdg-open) all carry bin_t; there is no separate
;; helper exec type to cover. Kept in its own module so it can be loaded or
;; rolled back independently of keepassxc_extras.

(typetransition keepassxc_t bin_t process staff_t)
(allow keepassxc_t bin_t (file (execute)))
(allow keepassxc_t staff_t (process (transition rlimitinh siginh noatsecure)))
